{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491151-dav20-dark-thaumaturgy-vs-thaumaturgy-vs-mauve-thaumaturgy","id":1491151,"title":"[DAV20] Dark Thaumaturgy vs Thaumaturgy vs Mauve Thaumaturgy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-23T19:33:16-07:00","id":1491151,"title":"[DAV20] Dark Thaumaturgy vs Thaumaturgy vs Mauve Thaumaturgy","content":"In V20, specifically Dark Ages 20th, is Dark Thaumaturgy considered a separate Discipline from Thaumaturgy? <br /> Previously, in revised edition, there was some mention in one of the books that &quot;Dark&quot; Thaumaturgy was just Thaumaturgy taught by demons, but since V20 changed some things I don't know if this is still true or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T02:14:00-07:00","id":1491172,"title":"","content":"Yes DT is a different discipline RAW. IIRC RAW it's always bought at In-clan rates (x5) as opposed to countermagic or koldunic sorcery (Always at OoC x7 rates) <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Looking at character sheets I have the suspicion that other characters add their DT rating to their Th rating (say Ted Has Thaumaturgy 4 he'll probably have DT 5 but I think that shouldn't normally be the case unless it's a 4+1 deal because... why would he get 5 levels of something that's essentially the same as the discipline he's already got. <i>Why is this common?</i>)<br /> <br /> <br /> I houserule a lot with DT. For me there's no exclusive paths or rituals. DT is just there for a shortcut/ demon related drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T12:36:17-07:00","id":1491229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491151-dav20-dark-thaumaturgy-vs-thaumaturgy-vs-mauve-thaumaturgy?p=1491172#post1491172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes DT is a different discipline RAW. IIRC RAW it's always bought at In-clan rates (x5) as opposed to countermagic or koldunic sorcery (Always at OoC x7 rates)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but I didn't see anything about costs being different?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491151-dav20-dark-thaumaturgy-vs-thaumaturgy-vs-mauve-thaumaturgy?p=1491172#post1491172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at character sheets I have the suspicion that other characters add their DT rating to their Th rating (say Ted Has Thaumaturgy 4 he'll probably have DT 5 but I think that shouldn't normally be the case unless it's a 4+1 deal because... why would he get 5 levels of something that's essentially the same as the discipline he's already got. <i>Why is this common?</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that they're cumulative and what does that mean and if that's the case then why have it a separate Discipline? I'm even more confused now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491151-dav20-dark-thaumaturgy-vs-thaumaturgy-vs-mauve-thaumaturgy?p=1491172#post1491172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I houserule a lot with DT. For me there's no exclusive paths or rituals. DT is just there for a shortcut/ demon related drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why don't you just take the Paths as &quot;normal&quot; Thaumaturgy Paths, if that's the case?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T12:57:29-07:00","id":1491232,"title":"","content":"One of the problems with infernalism is that it changes every edition because the writers recognize it needs a rewrite and it's very rare for players to get the power so they've got free reign to rewrite it but because it touches on devils and ideas about absolute evil nobody can ever settle on one coherent vision because of various sensitivities. OG DA infernalism is very different from revised which is in turn very different from DA and there are big differences between dark ages and modern nights and.... <br /> <br /> So yeah, I possibly read that DT is x5 somewhere and it's stuck with me. I've also read that using Diamonion without being on the path of evil revelations requires virtue rolls to avoid degeneration and decided that was fucking stupid (specially since there are various other pro-devil/Baali paths) <br /> <br /> Working out how infernalism is supposed to work in the WoD is like using the occult knowledge: you've gotta read through at least four different books before deciding whats bullshit and what's true. <br /> <br /> <br /> RAW it's not cumulative I just had the suspicion looking at character sheets. <br /> <br /> RAW, the reason why you would want DT are as follows<br /> -Because it offers some very powerful paths/rituals you maybe can't get with other thaumaturgy<br /> -Possibly discounted XP rates. <br /> -In maybe one DA edition you could get points for infernal stuff by doing evil shit. Though this might exclude DT so I may be wrong. <br /> <br /> Fluff wise<br /> -because it's easier to learn than regular thaumaturgy. Demons are good teachers and their abilities pick up a lot of the practitioner's slack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}